  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cropontology.org/rdf/CO_357:3000021/55">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">The majority of floral buds have emerged from the buds but are closed. Flowers with petals: the majority of flower buds have emerged from the buds and are still closed, but the colour of the petals is visible. Male flowers in catkins: the catkins are at the end of lengthening, the scales begin to move apart. Other flowers: stamens begin to be visible.</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:altLabel xml:lang="en">55</ns1:altLabel>
