  <ns3:Class rdf:about="https://cropontology.org/rdf/CO_357:1000016">
    <ns1:definition xml:lang="en">Number of whorls whith 1 default (fork, ramicorn…). A whorl or verticil is an arrangement of at least 3 sepals, petals, leaves, stipules or branches that radiate from a single point and surround or wrap around the stem.</ns1:definition>
    <ns2:entity>whorl</ns2:entity>
