  <ns3:Class rdf:about="https://cropontology.org/rdf/CO_357:2000056">
    <ns1:definition xml:lang="en">To boil the cork, the 30×30 cm samples are submerged in water at approximately 90°C for 1 h. During the drying period of 72 h cork is kept protected from direct light. The marked positions are then measured for comparison with data obtained before boiling.</ns1:definition>
